From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:22:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 088/112] Filters: a filter switched on fades in from the dry
 signal linearly, per frame, in 320 samples

1.2.1's fade-in (Filter::updateBlend()) multiplied the dry share by 0.99 on
every interleaved sample: exponential, left and right weighted differently in
every frame, a stereo fade twice as fast as a mono one, and the last 0.1 %
jumped at once. Now: out = wet + (dry - wet) * left / 320, left counting down
per frame from 319 to 0 (int64, saturated), the same weight for both channels,
the last frame all wet; 320 samples (7.3 ms) like FilterSet's crossfades
(static_assert). The float state is gone; a zeroed filter (FilterSet::reset())
has no fade, as before.

Only a filter switched from off to on in a running voice or in the song / a
kit / an audio track fades (a new voice starts without one since #4635).
tests/filters filter_neutral fadein: linear law within 1.2 LSB, left = right,
bit-exact with the plain filter from frame 320 (the source before: off by up
to 10^8 LSB, left != right).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
